  "hints": [
    "When does the last node hear the signal? Think about the shortest travel time to each node.",
    "Run Dijkstra from `k`: a min-heap of `(time, node)`, starting with `(0, k)`. Pop the smallest time; if the node is already settled skip it, otherwise settle it and push its neighbours with `time + w`. The answer is the largest settled time, or `-1` if fewer than `n` nodes were settled.",
    "Parallel example: news spreading through a village by phone calls of different lengths reaches the last person at the time of the slowest *fastest* route; always continuing from whoever heard the news earliest finds those routes."
  ],
